                        "form": "ouvreuses"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d3c82af3-c593-34cf-88c3-5f94e1901e0a",
                        "entry_id": "f97a5037-eb8b-31d7-8e94-3d940130dc9e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "vrouw die in een theater of bioscoop de bezoekers naar hun plaatsen brengt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "beroep"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2d9a010-f434-4d9e-898b-8df9681130d3",
                                "sense_id": "d3c82af3-c593-34cf-88c3-5f94e1901e0a",
                                "text": "Druppelsgewijs komen we te weten dat Louki de dochter is van een onbekende vader en een ouvreuse in de Moulin Rouge, dat ze korte tijd getrouwd is geweest met een oudere man en telkens weer alle bruggen opblaast, alle banden verbreekt en haar schepen achter zich verbrandt, eeuwig op de vlucht voor zichzelf."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd1cace7-489d-4ade-a144-f4d249594362",
                                "sense_id": "d3c82af3-c593-34cf-88c3-5f94e1901e0a",
                                "text": "Zo is er de historie van Bep van der Heijden-Put, die 45 jaar lang ouvreuse was in Luxor. En naast actrice Joke Bruijs en burgemeester Aboutaleb schittert bijvoorbeeld ook Nico Deflers, die als 15-jarig jochie meehielp om het puin van het bombardement op te ruimen."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0b11f50d-936f-4901-be1e-f52bb973d530",
                        "source_entry_id": "f97a5037-eb8b-31d7-8e94-3d940130dc9e",
                        "source_sense_id": "d3c82af3-c593-34cf-88c3-5f94e1901e0a",
                        "source_sense_description": "vrouw die in een theater of bioscoop de bezoekers naar hun plaatsen brengt",
                        "target_lang_word": "usherette",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "usherette",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7eda5c83-cdc5-33c3-9847-a9ae05e0b696",
                                        "entry_id": "5ad75c14-116e-3b41-af1b-3cda55cec100",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female usher."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db558d08-3058-404d-9636-a8a487f9ce4c",
                                                "sense_id": "7eda5c83-cdc5-33c3-9847-a9ae05e0b696",
                                                "text": "It is such a tiny little place that at first I thought I had gone wrong, and was in an antechamber. Plain papered walls, ascetic chairs, a moldy piano, and a couple of usherettes seemed extremely bare."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27c5cd0e-b853-4f40-b85f-a492eb3c8a7f",
                                                "sense_id": "7eda5c83-cdc5-33c3-9847-a9ae05e0b696",
                                                "text": "And then the usherette opened the doors of this dark palace and with a flashlight held behind her took him to his seat."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ea9a859-fa50-4cec-99cb-9f741bda3e68",
                                                "sense_id": "7eda5c83-cdc5-33c3-9847-a9ae05e0b696",
                                                "text": "He says, “Mike, let's do the town.” Can you refuse a guy who just gives you a thirty thousand dollar property? We do the town. We do the girl shows, and he yells at all the dames and tries to date the usherettes until we finally get pitched out. […]”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa64b004-03d3-4fe1-8b2a-f9a1a46223d4",
                                                "sense_id": "7eda5c83-cdc5-33c3-9847-a9ae05e0b696",
                                                "text": "[…] I won’t even see her again till next Saturday night on account of her doing week-nights as an usherette at the Regal […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1cb6b36f-3114-48c9-b4b7-b49b363e96bb",
                                                "sense_id": "7eda5c83-cdc5-33c3-9847-a9ae05e0b696",
                                                "text": "But please don’t call them usherettes. […] “Usherette makes us sound as if we’re miniature ushers or something. It’s an old term that we’re trying to get rid of.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
